            "answer": "Positional encodings are added to the input embeddings using sine and cosine functions of varying frequencies. For each position `pos` and dimension `i` the encoding is computed as  \n\n\\[\nPE(pos,2i) = \\sin\\!\\left(\\frac{pos}{10000^{\\,2i/d_{\\text{model}}}}\\right), \\qquad\nPE(pos,2i+1) = \\cos\\!\\left(\\frac{pos}{10000^{\\,2i/d_{\\text{model}}}}\\right).\n\\]\n\nThese functions produce a set of sinusoidal values whose wavelengths form a geometric progression from \\(2\\pi\\) to \\(10000 \\cdot 2\\pi\\).",
